  "description": "<p>When creating an ACL with PUT and an RDF body with undefined prefix, Fedora returns a stacktrace to the client.</p>\n\n<p>To reproduce:</p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Create resource:<br/>\ncurl -i -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/test\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/test</a> -XPUT</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Create ACL:<br/>\ncurl -i -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/test/fcr:acl\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/test/fcr:acl</a> -XPUT -H\"Content-Type: text/turtle\" --data-binary @body.ttl</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p>..where body.ttl is:<br/>\n&lt;&gt; a junk:Object ;</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li>BOOM!<br/>\nNotice: When creating a non-ACL RDF-Source with the same \"body.ttl\", no stacktrace is returned.</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
